  --no-worktree                       Branch in place instead of a git worktree
  --verdict-regex <re>                Reviewer verdict regex (default: '^VERDICT: (PASS|FAIL)')
  --preview | --no-preview            Force website preview+e2e on/off (else target config)
  --app-port <n> / --db-port <n>      Fixed preview ports (else auto-allocated)
  --preview-host <host>               Hostname for the preview URL (default: localhost)
  --keep-preview-on-fail              Leave the preview running after a failed run
  --run latest|<run-id>               Select a run for status/integrate/cleanup
  --force                             integrate non-ready / overwrite on install / force cleanup
  --delete-branch                     also delete the run branch (cleanup/integrate/--merged)
  --keep-worktree | --skip-cleanup    integrate: don't auto-clean up afterwards
  --pr                                integrate via pull request: push branch + gh pr create
                                      (Fixes #N from branch name; set RALPH_FIXES="1 3 4"
                                       to close multiple issues, e.g. a bundled batch run)
                                      (keeps the branch, removes the worktree; needs gh)
  --merged                            cleanup: remove every worktree whose PR is already merged (needs gh)
  --type generic|nextjs-postgres      init-target scaffold type

Batch options (ralph batch):
  --plan <dir|file>                   Tasks: a dir of *.md (sorted) or one .md split by heading
  --max-tasks <n>                     Cap how many tasks run (default: all)
  --max-iterations <n>                Per-task builder/reviewer attempts (default: 5)
  --verify <cmd>                      Acceptance gate run ONCE per task when check passes + reviewer PASSes
                                      (heavier than --check; a non-zero verify sends the task back to iterate)
  --primer <file>                     Repo-orientation text injected into every builder prompt ({{PRIMER}})
  --auto-approve-builder              Builder runs unattended (permission-skipping); reviewer stays read-only

Agent selection (ralph batch / review) — compose a backend from {provider,model,effort}:
  --profile cheap|balanced|max        Preset per-role provider/effort (fills unset knobs)
  --builder-provider <p>              codex | claude | zai|zlaude | opencode | droid  (reviewer: --reviewer-provider)
